<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $252 mln in Jan 22 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $252 mln in Jan 22 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $252 million to $43,319 million in the week ended January 22, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $244 million to $43,546 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $3,873 million to $806,329 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
